				<td width="100%">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#720">Charter For The Fellowship Of The Wolf</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							Firstly, a quick note before I talk about our wonderful guild. The Fellowship Of The Wolf recognises the fact that Everquest is ONLY a game. We are here to have fun, make friends and enjoy ourselves immensely. Everquest is a fantasy world, and should not be confused with real life. Thank you.<br />
<br />
The Fellowship Of The Wolf is a guild steeped in tradition. Formerly known as the Knights Of The Ebon Wolves, we are a guild that has been around for a long time, and has seen many changes and difficulties. We have overcome all these events to become the guild that we are today. Members have come and gone. History has been made, events have shaped us, and we are now stronger than we have ever been before.<br />
<br />
Our main reason for existence is to be a family. We are there for one another, in good times and bad. We are a pack. We all have a common bond and purpose. We are there to hunt together, to grieve together, to play together and most importantly to have fun together! We have a great family spirit going on right now. A great group of officers who will help anyone they can. We are growing and getting stronger, with the aim to be one of the greatest and most respected guilds in Norrath.<br />
<br />
We do not tolerate evil actions in anyone. We as a guild accept all races and classes, we do not discriminate. As long as all of our family are honorable, and selfless in their actions. A true wolf would sacrifice him or herself for the pack, if it meant doing so would save another’s life. Therefore we must all treat our fellow wolves as our equals, no matter what they’re standing. No fighting, bickering or rudeness will be tolerated. Respect, honour and love are the principles that we found our guild on.<br />
<br />
The following rules and regulations are needed to be met and followed to be able to become a member of The Fellowship Of The Wolf:-<br />
<br />
The person inviting them into the guild must direct anyone wishing to join the guild to this page and charter. They MUST NOT be signed up until they have read and understood what exactly it is we stand for.<br />
<br />
1. All races and classes are accepted by the guild. Evil actions will not be tolerated however.<br />
<br />
2. We currently have a level 10 restriction in place before you can join the Wolves. We feel that you need some time to develop your skills and abilities, and yourself as a person, before you would be an asset and family member of the pack. There are however a couple of exceptions to this rule for Clerics and Enchanters. We are screaming out for these two classes and as a result, these two classes can join us at level 5.<br />
<br />
3. A period of one month’s probation is in place for any new member. This is just to make sure that you are an honorable member of our family, and that you bear no ill wishes to any of the wolves.<br />
<br />
4. Our primary language in the guild is Elven. If you cannot speak this language at master level when you join us, get someone to teach you the language so you can speak it fluently.<br />
<br />
5. The guild is always looking to do good deeds for all. Do what you can, when you can for strangers. This is obviously in effect only if the help is not against actions that the Fellowship believes in.<br />
<br />
6. We are always happy to recruit new members. Speak to an officer if you find someone worthy that you wish to invite and that you feel will be an asset to our family.<br />
<br />
7. No rudeness, disrespect or selfish actions will be tolerated at all. A warning will be given, followed by an instant dismissal from the guild if more than half of the officers are in agreement on the matter.<br />
<br />
8. Treat others as you yourself wish to be treated.<br />
<br />
9. Most important rule. HAVE FUN! We are here to have a really good time. If you are here to moan and annoy people, find another guild that wants you!<br />
<br />
<br />
Thanks all.<br />
<br />
Lindias Lothlarien<br />
Druid Of Tunare<br />
Leader of The Fellowship Of The Wolf
